  {
    "episode_id": 81549,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/1/81549.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 1,
    "turn_text": "Welcome to the Advanced Colorado rundown. I'm Sean Duffy. I'm the Vice President at Advanced Colorado, and we are very pleased to be joined today by George Brockler, who is the Owens Early Fellow at the Common Sense Institute. He talks about criminal justice issues and crime issues, which is our topic today. George is the former 18th Judicial District Attorney. and very well respected all over our state and also the host every morning. Must listen radio show on K and U.S. AM and Denver. So, George, welcome. Thanks for being with us. Thanks for having me. We want to talk a little bit about crime and the Colorado Free Enterprise Report that the Common Sense Institute put out just a week ago. And in fact, the whole section, George, that you've been part of and and helped author talks about Colorado's performance on public safety and crime, and we didn't get really great grades.",
